Description: Self-hosted cloud platform with native FUSE and S3 sync
 Vaulthalla is a modern self-hosted cloud storage platform designed as
 a high-performance alternative to Nextcloud. It features a C++ core
 daemon, native Linux filesystem via FUSE, S3-compatible object storage,
 PostgreSQL indexing, and a secure web frontend. Vaulthalla emphasizes
 speed, sovereignty, and deep system integration for power users.

Package: vaulthalla-preview-cad
Architecture: any
Build-Profiles: <!pkg.vaulthalla.nocad>
Depends:
 vaulthalla (= ${binary:Version}),
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends}
Description: Vaulthalla STEP/STP preview converter
 Optional helper for the Vaulthalla daemon that converts STEP and STP CAD
 models into binary glTF (GLB) for the web console's 3D viewer. Built on
 Open CASCADE.
 .
 The daemon runs it out of process, one process per conversion, under
 resource limits, Landlock and a seccomp filter. Without this package
 STEP files are listed and downloadable but have no 3D preview.

Package: vaulthalla-preview-media
Architecture: any
Build-Profiles: <!pkg.vaulthalla.nomedia>
Depends:
 vaulthalla (= ${binary:Version}),
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends}
Description: Vaulthalla video and audio preview converter
 Optional helper for the Vaulthalla daemon that probes media files and
 produces poster frames and browser-playable transcodes with FFmpeg's
 libraries.
 .
 The daemon runs it out of process under resource limits, Landlock and a
 seccomp filter. Without this package media that browsers can play natively
 still streams; posters and transcodes are unavailable.
